# Hyperliquid Perpetuals

Lux provides transport-neutral Hyperliquid helpers for request planning,
position tracking, risk monitoring, liquidation buffers, margin summaries, and
safe execution decisions.

These helpers do not submit live orders or handle private keys.

## Info Requests

```elixir
alias Lux.Integrations.Hyperliquid.Perpetuals

Perpetuals.info_request(:meta)
Perpetuals.info_request(:clearinghouse_state, %{user: "0xabc"})
Perpetuals.info_request(:open_orders, %{user: "0xabc"})
Perpetuals.info_request(:all_mids)
```

## Order Plans

```elixir
Perpetuals.order_plan(%{
  coin: "ETH",
  side: :buy,
  size: 1.5,
  limit_px: 3_100,
  reduce_only: true,
  idempotency_key: "order-1"
})
```

## Position Snapshots

```elixir
position = %{
  coin: "ETH",
  size: 2.0,
  entry_px: 3_000.0,
  mark_px: 3_200.0,
  liquidation_px: 2_700.0,
  margin_used: 1_200.0,
  leverage: 5.0
}

Perpetuals.position_snapshot(position)
```

## Liquidation and Risk

```elixir
Perpetuals.liquidation_buffer(position)

Perpetuals.risk_decision(position, %{
  max_leverage: 6,
  min_liquidation_buffer: 0.1
})
```

## Margin Summary

```elixir
Perpetuals.margin_summary([position])
```

## Execution Decision

```elixir
Perpetuals.execution_decision(
  %{coin: "ETH", side: :buy, size: 1.0, limit_px: 3_100},
  position,
  %{max_leverage: 6}
)
```

Wire the returned order plans into signer/API adapters only after policy checks
pass.
